From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 13:58:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] third_party: vendor Stylo with the eager pseudo-element
 cascade skip

Build the Stylo crates from third_party/stylo through a
`[patch."https://github.com/servo/stylo"]` table instead of the git
dependency. The `git = ..., rev = ...` lines keep the upstream pin exactly
as upstream Servo writes them, and third_party/patches/stylo/update.sh
reads that pin: it fetches servo/stylo at the pinned commit, applies the
patches next to it and copies the tracked files (minus upstream's CI and
git configuration) into third_party/stylo, so an upstream bump of the pin
only needs a re-run of the script. `update.sh --export-patches`
regenerates the patches from a Stylo checkout and `update.sh --check`
verifies the committed copy. The whole of third_party is now excluded
from the workspace; the nested Stylo workspace manifest is needed for its
crates' `workspace = true` fields.

Stylo was the only git dependency, so the `servo` entry in cargo-deny's
allowed git organizations goes with it: cargo-deny warns about allowed
organizations without a git source and test-tidy treats that as an error.

The one patch, also proposed upstream, skips cascading the style of a
::before/::after whose matched rules declare no `content`. Such a
pseudo-element cannot generate a box, so Stylo threw the cascaded style
away; universal rules like Tailwind's `*, ::before, ::after { --tw-...: ... }`
made that half of all style traversal work on the GenUI pages. On the
PLR-AL00 with `--pref=layout_threads=1` (two A/B rounds, 20 loads each)
`layout_proper` drops by 16% (chuxing), 17% (biyadi), 26% (shibashiji)
and 16% (keai), and `traverse_dom` by 41-47%; the default three layout
threads confirm it. Rendering is unchanged: the same pseudo-elements were
already discarded after the cascade.

Validation: `third_party/patches/stylo/update.sh --check` reproduces the
committed copy. `./mach check --ohos`, `./mach fmt` and `./mach test-tidy`
pass. With the same Stylo patch as a path dependency, `./mach test-wpt
--release css/css-pseudo css/css-content css/cssom css/css-transitions
css/css-animations css/css-nesting css/css-lists css/selectors
css/css-cascade css/css-variables` runs with no unexpected results.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written and tested by the agent)

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
